---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
export const prerender = true;
---
<Base title="Sentinel-Bench — About" active="about">
  <main class="about-page-wrap">
    
    <!-- HERO SPLIT SECTION -->
    <section class="about-hero-grid">
      <div class="about-hero-text">
        <h1>Vulnerability tracking for <span class="green-accent">CTI professionals</span></h1>
        <p>
          Sentinel-Bench is a <strong>Cyber Threat Intelligence</strong> lab that aggregates, prioritizes, and consolidates vulnerabilities from public sources (CISA KEV, NVD, EPSS, GHSA, MSRC), ranked by real-world exploitation evidence.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-cta-btns">
          <a href="/dashboard/" class="btn-primary-hero">Explore Feed</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/iamtweaks/sentinel-bench" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn-secondary-hero">GitHub Repo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- TERMINAL PREVIEW WINDOW -->
      <div class="terminal-window">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="terminal-dot red"></div>
          <div class="terminal-dot yellow"></div>
          <div class="terminal-dot green"></div>
          <span style="font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);margin-left:8px">ingest.py — CLI</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body"><span style="color:var(--accent)">$ python -m ingest.ingest --source=KEV,EPSS,GHSA</span>
[+] Ingesting CISA KEV... 1,240 exploited CVEs fetched.
[+] Fetching EPSS scores... 2,000 top probabilities loaded.
[+] Normalizing & deduplicating vulnerabilities...
[+] Scoring Engine v1: recalculated 2,000 risk scores.
<span style="color:#38bdf8">[+] Top Threat: CVE-2025-20352 (Score: 94.2) -> Briefing generated.</span>
<span style="color:var(--muted)">[+] Supabase RLS sync complete. Dashboard ready.</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STATS GRID -->
    <section class="stats-grid">
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-num">2.0k+</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">Vulnerabilities</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-num" style="color:#38bdf8">1.2k</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">CISA KEV Catalog</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-num" style="color:#f59e0b">850+</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">Public PoCs</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-box">
        <div class="stat-num" style="color:#a78bfa">5</div>
        <div class="stat-lbl">Intel Sources</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- METHODOLOGY & DETAILS CARD -->
    <section class="about-card">
      <h2>Mission</h2>
      <p>
        Monitor vulnerabilities in real time based on <strong>objective evidence of active exploitation</strong>, instead of relying solely on the traditional CVSS metric. We unify open public feeds into a single interactive feed and send daily alerts via Telegram when the Top 5 changes.
      </p>

      <h2>Integrated Open Sources</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>CISA KEV</strong> — Catalog of vulnerabilities with confirmed exploitation in the wild.</li>
        <li><strong>NVD CVE 2.0</strong> — National Vulnerability Database (CVSS v3, CPEs, descriptions).</li>
        <li><strong>FIRST EPSS</strong> — Probabilistic model estimating 30-day exploit likelihood.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub Security Advisories (GHSA)</strong> — Community-curated advisories and PoC references.</li>
        <li><strong>Microsoft MSRC</strong> — Official security updates for the Microsoft infrastructure.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Deterministic Scoring Formula (0–100)</h2>
      <p>No dependence on LLM hallucinations for score assignment. The calculation combines:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>30 pts</strong> × Presence in CISA KEV</li>
        <li><strong>25 pts</strong> × EPSS percentile ≥ 99%</li>
        <li><strong>15 pts</strong> × EPSS Score ≥ 50%</li>
        <li><strong>12 pts</strong> × CVSS v3 proportional (/10)</li>
        <li><strong>8 pts</strong> × Exploit evidence (Confirmed / PoC / Likely)</li>
        <li><strong>5 pts</strong> × Vulnerability recency (&lt;7d / &lt;30d / &lt;90d)</li>
        <li><strong>3 pts</strong> × Multi-source corroboration</li>
        <li><strong>2 pts</strong> × High-exposure vendor in infrastructure</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Transparency and Privacy Guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        🔒 <strong>100% Public Intelligence</strong>. Isolated from any corporate network or private SOC. It does not scrape internal infrastructure or contain confidential IoCs. Designed as a professional Blue Team / Cyber Threat Intelligence portfolio.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
